    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Run AI matting on a video or photo segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --feather TEXT      Matting edge feather, e.g. 10\r\n          --expansion TEXT    Matting edge expansion, e.g. 5\r\n          --reverse           Reverse the algorithm effect where supported\r\n          --wait TEXT         Wait for the algorithm to finish: true / false (default true)\r\n          --workspace TEXT    Matting output directory (alias of `path`); defaults to\r\n                              matting/<md5> next to the source video\r\n          --config-path TEXT  Override the algorithm config directory\r\n          --cancel            Cancel AI matting instead of starting a new task\r\n          --video-new-use-model TEXT \r\n                              Use the newer ai_matting_gru model: true / false (must match the\r\n                              on-device AB switch)\r\n          --photo-new-use-model TEXT \r\n                              Use the newer photo matting model: true / false\r\n          --use-algorithm-path TEXT \r\n                              Use algorithm product path: true / false\r\n          --face-detect-interval <duration> \r\n                              Video face-detection interval; explicit unit required (us, ms, s,\r\n                              min; default 1s)\r\n          --face-detect-limit TEXT \r\n                              Video face-detection limit (default 60)\r\n          --face-threshold TEXT \r\n                              Video face-detection threshold (default 0.5)\r\n          --commit-immediately TEXT \r\n                              Commit the matting draft change immediately: true / false\r\n                              (default true)\r\n          --reuse-existing TEXT \r\n                              Reuse an existing valid matting product: true / false\r\n          --reuse-from-segment-id TEXT \r\n                              Prefer the matting product attached to this segment id\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Cut out the subject, softening and expanding the matte edge\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --feather 10 --expansion 5\r\n  # Invert the matte (keep background instead of subject)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --reverse\r\n  # Cancel matting, or point at a custom workspace / config dir\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --cancel\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --workspace /tmp/matting --config-path /tmp/cfg --wait false\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Run AI matting on a video or photo segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --feather TEXT      Matting edge feather, e.g. 10\r\n          --expansion TEXT    Matting edge expansion, e.g. 5\r\n          --reverse           Reverse the algorithm effect where supported\r\n          --wait TEXT         Wait for the algorithm to finish: true / false (default true)\r\n          --workspace TEXT    Matting output directory (alias of `path`); defaults to\r\n                              matting/<md5> next to the source video\r\n          --config-path TEXT  Override the algorithm config directory\r\n          --cancel            Cancel AI matting instead of starting a new task\r\n          --video-new-use-model TEXT \r\n                              Use the newer ai_matting_gru model: true / false (must match the\r\n                              on-device AB switch)\r\n          --photo-new-use-model TEXT \r\n                              Use the newer photo matting model: true / false\r\n          --use-algorithm-path TEXT \r\n                              Use algorithm product path: true / false\r\n          --face-detect-interval <duration> \r\n                              Video face-detection interval; explicit unit required (us, ms, s,\r\n                              min; default 1s)\r\n          --face-detect-limit TEXT \r\n                              Video face-detection limit (default 60)\r\n          --face-threshold TEXT \r\n                              Video face-detection threshold (default 0.5)\r\n          --commit-immediately TEXT \r\n                              Commit the matting draft change immediately: true / false\r\n                              (default true)\r\n          --reuse-existing TEXT \r\n                              Reuse an existing valid matting product: true / false\r\n          --reuse-from-segment-id TEXT \r\n                              Prefer the matting product attached to this segment id\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Cut out the subject, softening and expanding the matte edge\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --feather 10 --expansion 5\r\n  # Invert the matte (keep background instead of subject)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --reverse\r\n  # Cancel matting, or point at a custom workspace / config dir\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --cancel\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-matting --seg-id <UUID> --workspace /tmp/matting --config-path /tmp/cfg --wait false\r\n",
